com/image/fetch/$s_!57HP!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F2f855cc1-d52c-4cd8-8c78-018f98b307d1_1424x823.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!57HP!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F2f855cc1-d52c-4cd8-8c78-018f98b307d1_1424x823.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!57HP!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F2f855cc1-d52c-4cd8-8c78-018f98b307d1_1424x823.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!57HP!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F2f855cc1-d52c-4cd8-8c78-018f98b307d1_1424x823.png 1456w\" sizes=\"auto, 100vw\" loading=\"lazy\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a><figcaption class=\"image-caption\">VIX can stay below “14” for lengthy periods of time. Don’t get married to any single number, focus more on trends. </figcaption></figure></div><div><hr></div><h4>Timothy’s Plan Going Forward</h4><p>As always, we update day to day. Anything can happen. A meteor could hit Wall Street tomorrow, and we would have to adjust our plan. </p><p>But the bigger picture hasn’t changed. I still believe we are in the blow-off top I’ve been preparing for over the last four years. We got the melt-up. Now I’m becoming increasingly selective about where I am willing to put money. </p><p>Yesterday I sold off most of our regional banks, WSFS, CATY and SPG, a sector I have been bullish on since the beginning of the year. Locking in 32%, 17% and 11% respectively. </p><h4>So where is that money going now?</h4><h4>There is one stock I am planning to buy today, and a very specific approach in the coming weeks, that is unlike my norm…</h4>",
